&lt;h3&gt;Added&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstros updates itself.&lt;/b&gt; It checks for a new version once a day and offers it in a window with what's new. Installing asks for your admin password, as the installer does, and Abstros reopens once on the new version. Choose Abstros › Check for Updates… (also in the menu bar icon's menu) to look now. Updates are signed: Abstros installs only a package signed with the Abstros update key and notarized by Apple.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Updates never interrupt a session.&lt;/b&gt; While you're on a call, recording or live, a new version is only noted ("Update to 0.4.x…" in the menus, a banner in Settings) and offered once you're free. An update you accepted mid-session waits before it quits and reopens Abstros.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Update settings&lt;/b&gt; in Settings › System › Updates: check automatically, download in the background, Stable or Beta versions, when it last checked, and Check Now.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Changed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branded installers.&lt;/b&gt; The installer shows the Abstros mark in its sidebar, in light and dark, with restyled welcome and finish pages. The finish page says future updates come through the app.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branded microphone packages.&lt;/b&gt; The Abstros Microphone install and uninstall packages that Settings opens are now proper installers with the same branding and short explanations, not bare packages.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;One launch after an update.&lt;/b&gt; When the update installs from the app, the installer leaves reopening Abstros to the updater, so it opens once.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
